        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1a6c1b43-a5df-594a-abc4-3c2f0f2227c2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Kickin' It\n- People: Jim O'Doherty, Jason Earles, Leo Howard, Dylan Riley Snyder, Olivia Holt\n- Organizations: Disney XD, Guinness World Records\n- Topics: television series, martial arts, comedy, directing records\n\nFacts:\n- Kickin' It is an American martial arts-inspired comedy television series that aired on Disney XD from June 13, 2011 to March 25, 2015.\n- Jim O'Doherty created and executive produced Kickin' It.\n- Kickin' It follows a karate instructor at an under-performing martial arts academy, played by Jason Earles, and five misfit students, including characters played by Leo Howard, Dylan Riley Snyder, and Olivia Holt.\n- In the fourth season of Kickin' It, Leo Howard directed the episode \"Fight at the Museum\" at age 16.\n- Guinness World Records certified Leo Howard as the youngest TV director ever for his work on the Kickin' It episode \"Fight at the Museum.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
